{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואספתו", :translit "v'asafto", :gloss "and you shall gather it"} {:he "ואספתו מצרעתו", :translit "v'asafto mitzora'ato", :gloss "and you shall gather him from his leprosy"} {:he "ואספתו אל תוך ביתך", :translit "v'asafto el toch beitecha", :gloss "and you shall gather it into your house"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואספתו" "ואספתו מצרעתו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking two forms of ואספתו to derive that stinginess causes tzara'at"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that tzara'at afflictions come upon a stingy person who refuses to lend his vessels and claims he has nothing; when the priest orders the house cleared for inspection, all his vessels are exposed (Arakhin 16a). The Talmud (Shabbat 97a) also teaches that one who suspects the worthy is stricken with tzara'at. By returning the lost item, one removes the owner's suspicion and thereby spares him from this affliction.", :sources ["Arakhin 16a" "Shabbat 97a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "עד דרוש אחיך אותו", :translit "ad d'rosh achicha oto", :gloss "until your brother seeks it"} {:he "דרשהו", :translit "darshuhu", :gloss "seek him / examine him"} {:he "בסימנים שעליה", :translit "b'simanim she'aleiha", :gloss "by the signs upon it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reads דרוש as 'investigate' — require identifying signs before returning a lost item"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud derives that a finder must examine whether the claimant is trustworthy; the criterion is whether the claimant can provide identifying signs on the lost object (Bava Metzia 28b).", :sources ["Bava Metzia 28b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואספתו" "ואספתו מצרעתו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואספתו", :refs ["Deuteronomy 22:2" "2 Kings 5:6"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ואספתו מצרעתו", :refs ["2 Kings 5:6"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking two forms of ואספתו to derive that stingi